(SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE BOARD OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(CORPORATION FINANCE DEPARTMENT, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(SEBI/HO/CFD/PoD-1/P/CIR/2024/152) Tj
T*
(September 23, 2024) Tj
T*
(Framework for Social Stock Exchange \(SSE\) - Registration and Instrument Issuance) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Social Stock Exchange Ecosystem: The Social Stock Exchange \(SSE\) functions as a separate segment of recognized stock exchanges to enable) Tj
T*
(Social Enterprises to raise capital for public welfare activities across 16 eligible social sectors, including poverty eradication, healthcare,) Tj
T*
(education, and environmental sustainability.) Tj
T*
(2. Eligible Social Enterprises: Entities eligible to register on the SSE include Non-Profit Organisations \(NPOs\) and For-Profit Social) Tj
T*
(Enterprises \(FPSEs\). To be eligible, at least 67 percent of the entity's revenues or activities in the preceding three years must be directed) Tj
T*
(towards serving target underserved populations.) Tj
T*
(3. Zero Coupon Zero Principal \(ZCZP\) Instruments: NPOs registered on the SSE may raise funds through the issuance of Zero Coupon Zero Principal) Tj
T*
(\(ZCZP\) instruments. ZCZP instruments carry no interest or coupon payments and have no principal repayment obligations.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 900 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Issue Size and Subscription Limits: The minimum issue size for issuance of ZCZP instruments on the Social Stock Exchange is rupees) Tj
T*
(fifty lakh \(INR 50,00,000\). The minimum application size for both retail and institutional investors is rupees ten thousand \(INR 10,000\).) Tj
T*
(5. Social Audit Requirement: All social enterprises registered on or listed on the SSE must undergo an annual Social Audit conducted by an) Tj
T*
(independent Social Audit Firm employing certified Social Auditors empanelled with the Institute of Social Auditors of India \(ISAI\). The Social) Tj
T*
(Audit Report must be submitted to the stock exchange within 60 calendar days from the end of each financial year.) Tj
T*
(6. Validity of NPO Registration: NPO registration on the SSE remains valid for three years and is renewable upon submission of audited financials.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 805 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. Annual Impact Report Contents: The Social Audit Report must evaluate strategic intent, social problem addressed, systemic change) Tj
T*
(theories, input-output ratios, and qualitative feedback from beneficiaries. It must verify whether target outcomes were achieved.) Tj
T*
(8. For-Profit Social Enterprises \(FPSEs\): FPSEs may raise equity capital through public issuance on the Main Board or SME Platform, or issue debt) Tj
T*
(securities, while voluntarily adhering to the Social Audit and reporting frameworks of the SSE.) Tj
T*
(9. Development Impact Bonds \(DIBs\): NPOs may participate in DIB structures where funding is provided upfront by risk investors and repaid by) Tj
T*
(Outcome Funders upon independent verification of social milestones achieved.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 764 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. De-Registration from SSE: An NPO may be delisted from the Social Stock Exchange if it fails to submit annual social audit reports) Tj
T*
(for two consecutive financial years or if its tax exemption under Section 12A/12AB of the Income Tax Act is cancelled.) Tj
T*
(11. Minimum Public Float: NPOs issuing ZCZP instruments must ensure that the minimum public float is achieved within thirty days of issue closure.) Tj
T*
(12. Governing Board Requirements: The governing board of an NPO listed on the SSE must comprise at least three trustees or directors, with no single) Tj
T*
(family member controlling more than fifty percent of voting rights.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Yogita Jadhav\)) Tj
T*
(General Manager) Tj
T*
